      "headings": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Cell P01.1 — CoordinationSession store, schema, events, direct cutover (Phase 01 R1-R4)",
          "anchor": "cell-p011-coordinationsession-store-schema-events-direct-cutover-phase-01-r1-r4",
          "githubAnchor": "cell-p011-coordinationsession-store-schema-events-direct-cutover-phase-01-r1-r4",
          "stableAnchor": "h-258d4eb4c120"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Requirements",
          "anchor": "requirements",
          "githubAnchor": "requirements",
          "stableAnchor": "h-f5d328743132"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Proof Matrix",
          "anchor": "proof-matrix",
          "githubAnchor": "proof-matrix",
          "stableAnchor": "h-cffbfc73cd1e"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Commands",
          "anchor": "commands",
          "githubAnchor": "commands",
          "stableAnchor": "h-5591f6bc2e72"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Doer Judgment Calls",
          "anchor": "doer-judgment-calls",
          "githubAnchor": "doer-judgment-calls",
          "stableAnchor": "h-aa3de297b2a7"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Review",
          "anchor": "review",
          "githubAnchor": "review",
          "stableAnchor": "h-feb23f496a94"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "HIGH — Crash-then-retry after an interrupted `assignment-created` write can duplicate the Assignment for one logical task, violating the contract's Required Negative Test #3",
          "anchor": "high-crash-then-retry-after-an-interrupted-assignment-created-write-can-duplicate-the-assignment-for-one-logical-task-violating-the-contracts-required-negative-test-3",
          "githubAnchor": "high-crash-then-retry-after-an-interrupted-assignment-created-write-can-duplicate-the-assignment-for-one-logical-task-violating-the-contracts-required-negative-test-3",
          "stableAnchor": "h-b68b3a0ea411"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "MEDIUM — Only `replaySession` checks `schemaVersion`; every mutating store operation (`createSessionAssignment`, `bindActor`, `linkResult`, `transitionSessionStatus`) reads the manifest via `readManifestRaw`, which never compares `schemaVersion` against the running `SCHEMA_VERSION`",
          "anchor": "medium-only-replaysession-checks-schemaversion-every-mutating-store-operation-createsessionassignment-bindactor-linkresult-transitionsessionstatus-reads-the-manifest-via-readmanifestraw-which-never-compares-schemaversion-against-the-running-schemaversion",
          "githubAnchor": "medium-only-replaysession-checks-schemaversion-every-mutating-store-operation-createsessionassignment-bindactor-linkresult-transitionsessionstatus-reads-the-manifest-via-readmanifestraw-which-never-compares-schemaversion-against-the-running-schemaversion",
          "stableAnchor": "h-9bff661546cf"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "LOW — Doer's \"no new failure beyond baseline\" full-suite claim did not reproduce exactly; one failure title not in the 11-item baseline surfaced on my own full-suite run",
          "anchor": "low-doers-no-new-failure-beyond-baseline-full-suite-claim-did-not-reproduce-exactly-one-failure-title-not-in-the-11-item-baseline-surfaced-on-my-own-full-suite-run",
          "githubAnchor": "low-doers-no-new-failure-beyond-baseline-full-suite-claim-did-not-reproduce-exactly-one-failure-title-not-in-the-11-item-baseline-surfaced-on-my-own-full-suite-run",
          "stableAnchor": "h-079e40033937"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Confirmed correct (verified independently, not merely re-trusting the Doer's claim)",
          "anchor": "confirmed-correct-verified-independently-not-merely-re-trusting-the-doers-claim",
          "githubAnchor": "confirmed-correct-verified-independently-not-merely-re-trusting-the-doers-claim",
          "stableAnchor": "h-c4e5c66a865b"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Verification commands run independently",
          "anchor": "verification-commands-run-independently",
          "githubAnchor": "verification-commands-run-independently",
          "stableAnchor": "h-f96b50850af8"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Red-Team",
          "anchor": "red-team",
          "githubAnchor": "red-team",
          "stableAnchor": "h-b060add1e7d9"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "HIGH — The accepted HIGH fix's own retry fast-path returns a \"successful\" Assignment that is never actually added to the session (no `assignment-created` event, no `assignmentRefs` entry), permanently, with no self-heal — reopening the exact contract requirement it was dispatched to close",
          "anchor": "high-the-accepted-high-fixs-own-retry-fast-path-returns-a-successful-assignment-that-is-never-actually-added-to-the-session-no-assignment-created-event-no-assignmentrefs-entry-permanently-with-no-self-heal-reopening-the-exact-contract-requirement-it-was-dispatched-to-close",
          "githubAnchor": "high-the-accepted-high-fixs-own-retry-fast-path-returns-a-successful-assignment-that-is-never-actually-added-to-the-session-no-assignment-created-event-no-assignmentrefs-entry-permanently-with-no-self-heal-reopening-the-exact-contract-requirement-it-was-dispatched-to-close",
          "stableAnchor": "h-d8f5dfd49275"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "MEDIUM — `sanitizeTaskKey`'s lossy sanitization lets two textually-distinct `taskKey`s collide onto the same claim file, silently dropping the second logical task's Assignment instead of creating it",
          "anchor": "medium-sanitizetaskkeys-lossy-sanitization-lets-two-textually-distinct-taskkeys-collide-onto-the-same-claim-file-silently-dropping-the-second-logical-tasks-assignment-instead-of-creating-it",
